#!/usr/bin/python3 -I
"""Classification of suspicious destinations for the Allowlist proxy.

Loaded by the proxy as a module and used by agentbox as a command:
  agentbox-suspicious <host>                 prints the Signals (empty = nothing suspicious);
                                             exit 2 on a strong Signal, exit 3 (reason on
                                             stderr) while the Watchlist cannot be read:
                                             which Signals are strong is then unknown
  agentbox-suspicious --json <host>          the Signals with reasons (agentbox check-domain)
  agentbox-suspicious --watchlist            the Watchlist and the state of the HaGeZi lists
                                             as JSON (agentbox watchlist)
  agentbox-suspicious --constants            the Watchlist categories (strong or not) and
                                             the built-in Legitimate domains as JSON
  agentbox-suspicious --lifts <domain>       what making the domain legitimate would lift:
                                             strong Signals (not the blockchain pattern,
                                             which stays) and entries of the Threat
                                             Intelligence list below it, as JSON
  agentbox-suspicious --signals <host>...    the Signals of each host and whether one is strong,
                                             and why the Watchlist cannot be read, as JSON (the
                                             preview of a regex Allowlist entry)
  agentbox-suspicious --self-test            self-test of the detection (agentbox setup): starts
                                             the proxy next to this file with test lists

Regex entries (ADR 0013): every list can hold a regular expression instead of a domain,
matched with re.fullmatch against the lowercased host without its trailing dot, and
compiled once whenever its file is read again. The rules a pattern has to follow are
in agentbox's list records (agentbox/list_records.py, pattern_problem), which this
program, the proxy and agentbox import alike. A regex Legitimate domain lifts only weak Signals: which strong
ones it would lift cannot be checked for a pattern (ADR 0009, ADR 0013).

Basis: an analysis of supply-chain incidents 2024-2026 (Shai-Hulud,
s1ngularity, chalk/debug, axios, TanStack, keyv, GlassWorm). Fixed domains
are on the Watchlist; the patterns here also catch domains that only become known
after an incident. False positives are accepted: a weak Signal only raises an
Alert. Strong Signals always block in the proxy, whatever would allow the destination: an
Allowlist entry, also a domain entry, or Open web (ADR 0021).

Lists (each including subdomains, read again on change without a restart; for the
Signals a broken file leaves the last good state, for the Watchlist also when it is
missing. While that one is broken or missing altogether, the proxy lets
nothing through, Allowlist entries included, and closes every tunnel):
  /etc/agentbox/watchlist.json       the Watchlist (agentbox watch-add/-remove),
                                     each entry with a category and a source
  /etc/agentbox/legitimate.json      known Legitimate domains (agentbox legitimate-add/
                                     -remove) and the built-in ones (GENUINE): no
                                     pattern Signals except the blockchain pattern, and HaGeZi
                                     list hits for them and below do not count (when
                                     classifying; the lists are unfiltered); except
                                     subdomains of the user-content domains (USER_CONTENT:
                                     github.io, githubusercontent.com, claudeusercontent.com),
                                     where any user can publish: their hits count
                                     Until agentbox migrate-lists creates it, the text files
                                     suspicious-domains and legitimate-domains (one domain
                                     per line) apply in its place.
  /etc/agentbox/harmless             marked harmless (agentbox mark-harmless): raises
                                     no more Alerts, but is otherwise unchanged
                                     (strong Signals keep blocking it);
                                     a line "regex <pattern>" is a Regex entry
  /var/lib/agentbox/feeds/           HaGeZi lists from agentbox-feeds (timer):
                                     threat-intelligence (Signal threat) and
                                     newly-registered (Signal young)
The HaGeZi lists have millions of entries. They lie sorted on disk
and are read with binary search through mmap: every proxy process shares the
pages with all others through the page cache and loads nothing into memory.
"""
import ipaddress
import json
import math
import mmap
import os
import re
import shutil
import socket
import subprocess
import sys
import tempfile
import time


def _package_dir():
    """Where the package agentbox is: next to proxy/ in a checkout, installed in lib/agentbox
    under the prefix whose libexec/ holds this program. This program and the proxy import only
    its leaf module list_records (tests/test_list_records.py)."""
    here = os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__)))
    checkout = os.path.isfile(os.path.join(here, "agentbox", "__init__.py"))
    return here if checkout else os.path.join(here, "lib", "agentbox")


if _package_dir() not in sys.path:
    sys.path.insert(0, _package_dir())
from agentbox import list_records as records  # noqa: E402
from agentbox import proxy_log  # noqa: E402
from agentbox.list_records import (CATEGORIES, PATTERN_HOST, STRONG, compile_pattern,  # noqa: E402,F401
                                   pattern_matches, pattern_problem, printable, refused_entry)

